1
00:02:03,940 --> 00:02:08,500
NO ANIMALS WERE HARMED DURING
THE FILMING OF THIS PRODUCTION

2
00:02:08,500 --> 00:02:38,420
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

3
00:02:38,700 --> 00:02:40,480
What are you up to this time, Targun?

4
00:02:41,280 --> 00:02:42,480
Drop your sword, Bala.

5
00:02:42,820 --> 00:02:44,260
I did nothing wrong.

6
00:02:44,580 --> 00:02:46,400
Osman Bey and I had a talk.

7
00:02:49,280 --> 00:02:51,900
But it's obvious that you are off to
something else.

8
00:03:02,180 --> 00:03:03,340
Targun!

9
00:03:03,940 --> 00:03:06,020
Are you trying to save your father?

10
00:03:06,560 --> 00:03:08,260
Or, to cause problems for us?

11
00:03:10,060 --> 00:03:11,200
Traitor!

12
00:03:14,620 --> 00:03:19,000
I told you'll understand whether I am
Azreal or the Hellhound, Osman.

13
00:03:27,700 --> 00:03:30,620
The life given by Allah...

14
00:03:31,680 --> 00:03:33,920
... can't be taken by anyone...

15
00:03:35,340 --> 00:03:37,740
... but Allah.

16
00:04:21,240 --> 00:04:23,060
What was written on that paper?

17
00:04:26,340 --> 00:04:27,280
Aygül...

18
00:04:30,500 --> 00:04:31,500
... it's a secret.

19
00:04:33,560 --> 00:04:35,880
I'm done with your secrets!

20
00:04:36,260 --> 00:04:38,540
Tell me what was written!

21
00:04:39,680 --> 00:04:41,780
How courages you three are.

22
00:04:43,800 --> 00:04:45,000
Leave us alone!

23
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:46,380
We shall talk one on one.

24
00:04:51,260 --> 00:04:52,520
It's enough, Aygül.

25
00:04:52,720 --> 00:04:54,720
I know how to make her speak.

26
00:04:55,200 --> 00:04:58,880
I can't leave you alone with this snake.

27
00:05:00,300 --> 00:05:01,840
Listen to my words, Aygül.

28
00:05:05,420 --> 00:05:07,640
If it wasn't for the sake of Osman Bey...

29
00:05:11,960 --> 00:05:14,920
... I'd chop her right here right now.

30
00:05:20,800 --> 00:05:23,180
Gonca. May you two go back to Tent now.

31
00:05:30,340 --> 00:05:31,880
I know your father is alive.

32
00:05:34,140 --> 00:05:35,960
And that he is a captive of Nikola.

33
00:05:37,520 --> 00:05:40,460
I know you are trying to play
games on Osman Bey.

34
00:05:42,600 --> 00:05:45,400
It's good that you know everything.

35
00:05:46,460 --> 00:05:50,100
I don't know what you are doing here
and what was written on that paper.

36
00:05:50,760 --> 00:05:51,980
But I will learn.

37
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:57,460
But I'd like you to tell me these not at
a forest like a traitor...

38
00:06:00,860 --> 00:06:03,220
... but at the Tent like a proper Hatun.

39
00:06:51,500 --> 00:06:52,900
You are right, Osman.

40
00:06:54,600 --> 00:06:56,840
God is the taker of lives.

41
00:07:01,320 --> 00:07:03,200
But God uses intermediaries.

42
00:07:05,720 --> 00:07:07,940
And he has assigned me to kill you.

43
00:07:09,820 --> 00:07:12,420
Sooner or later, you will pay for my
brother Ayaz.

44
00:07:20,840 --> 00:07:21,720
Sertaş.

45
00:08:56,540 --> 00:08:59,180
If you want to die while standing, so
be it, Osman.

46
00:09:02,340 --> 00:09:03,860
I respect that.

47
00:09:25,140 --> 00:09:26,360
For Rome!

48
00:09:40,520 --> 00:09:42,260
What are you doing?

49
00:09:42,500 --> 00:09:44,220
I'm going to kill him myself.

50
00:10:02,340 --> 00:10:04,120
Cerkutay is back!

51
00:10:17,740 --> 00:10:19,340
Today is the day of Flatyos!

52
00:10:35,440 --> 00:10:36,600
Sertaş!

53
00:11:16,820 --> 00:11:18,860
My Bey!

54
00:11:25,480 --> 00:11:27,360
Take your men and leave, Flatyos.

55
00:11:39,780 --> 00:11:40,820
My Bey!

56
00:11:45,860 --> 00:11:47,200
How magnificent!

57
00:11:47,720 --> 00:11:48,860
How wonderful!

58
00:11:50,800 --> 00:11:52,420
Thanks to Allah!

59
00:11:55,540 --> 00:11:56,580
Osman.

60
00:11:58,220 --> 00:11:59,400
My son.

61
00:12:00,600 --> 00:12:02,440
Where is my son, Osman?

62
00:12:05,620 --> 00:12:06,960
You can do it, my Bey.

63
00:12:07,200 --> 00:12:08,440
Bismillah.

64
00:12:09,820 --> 00:12:11,120
How wonderful.

65
00:12:14,620 --> 00:12:15,920
Praise be!

66
00:12:16,020 --> 00:12:20,020
I will give the news to our people, my
Bey.

67
00:12:22,500 --> 00:12:23,840
Don't, Abdurrahman.

68
00:12:26,220 --> 00:12:27,280
Don't tell them.

69
00:12:30,220 --> 00:12:34,740
If people ask, don't tell them that I'm
alright.

70
00:12:37,020 --> 00:12:43,160
I want to understand how they're doing
without me.

71
00:12:44,740 --> 00:12:48,960
When the time comes, I know what to do.

72
00:12:52,600 --> 00:12:54,280
As you wish, my Bey.

73
00:12:58,100 --> 00:13:00,300
I won't hand you even a single Turk!

74
00:13:01,360 --> 00:13:05,580
Just like I won't break the peace
agreement between us.

75
00:13:23,720 --> 00:13:25,180
Get out of my way, Yalvak.

76
00:13:26,480 --> 00:13:28,120
Osman is going to die!

77
00:13:32,720 --> 00:13:33,920
Take him away!

78
00:13:37,720 --> 00:13:39,760
Tell Nikola what happened.

79
00:13:40,220 --> 00:13:43,520
I didn't break the peace agreement
between us.

80
00:13:57,840 --> 00:14:00,780
Drop your swords, Alps!

81
00:14:04,520 --> 00:14:05,520
My Bey!

82
00:14:22,980 --> 00:14:24,540
Where is that dog?

83
00:14:29,420 --> 00:14:30,540
Where is that dog?

84
00:14:30,580 --> 00:14:32,080
I sent him off, Osman.

85
00:14:34,620 --> 00:14:37,820
I sticked to the peace agreement between
us and them.

86
00:14:38,100 --> 00:14:39,080
What?

87
00:14:39,880 --> 00:14:41,280
You sent him off?

88
00:14:41,440 --> 00:14:43,740
What are you talking about?

89
00:14:45,600 --> 00:14:47,300
The heathen has gone...

90
00:14:48,520 --> 00:14:50,480
... but his partner stayed, huh?

91
00:14:51,120 --> 00:14:53,460
Know that I saved your life, Osman!

92
00:14:53,720 --> 00:14:55,140
I saved you from death.

93
00:14:55,280 --> 00:14:57,360
You wanted to kill my brother and me!

94
00:15:00,540 --> 00:15:01,940
Don't barge in, Alps!

95
00:15:02,840 --> 00:15:03,740
Don't!

96
00:15:06,340 --> 00:15:07,400
You too!

97
00:15:15,140 --> 00:15:17,120
One of us is going to die today.

98
00:15:17,520 --> 00:15:19,240
Your treason must be punished!

99
00:15:20,400 --> 00:15:24,700
A partner of heathens can't be friends
with the ones fighting against them.

100
00:15:28,160 --> 00:15:30,400
So be it, Osman!

101
00:15:30,800 --> 00:15:35,720
Those who seek peace and those who seek
war but nothing else...

102
00:15:35,720 --> 00:15:38,260
... can't work together for a bigger
cause.

103
00:15:38,420 --> 00:15:39,780
Which cause is that?

104
00:15:40,800 --> 00:15:41,980
We'd like to know that!

105
00:15:43,560 --> 00:15:47,200
I will act like I work together with those
Romans you call heathens...

106
00:15:47,800 --> 00:15:50,340
... then I will kill the biggest heathen
there is.

107
00:15:54,160 --> 00:15:55,640
And who is that person?

108
00:15:58,220 --> 00:15:59,680
Which heathen?

109
00:16:02,660 --> 00:16:03,940
Which heathen!

110
00:16:23,540 --> 00:16:24,880
What's wrong, brother?

111
00:16:27,440 --> 00:16:29,780
Brother, huh?

112
00:16:34,620 --> 00:16:36,340
I know what you are up to, Savcı.

113
00:16:37,280 --> 00:16:38,540
You need to back down!

114
00:16:40,100 --> 00:16:41,600
Only for the good of Kayı...

115
00:16:41,600 --> 00:16:42,760
Stop!

116
00:16:44,740 --> 00:16:46,360
Enough already.

117
00:16:48,060 --> 00:16:50,960
By the good of Kayı, you only mean your
ambitions!

118
00:16:52,400 --> 00:16:57,860
Let me tell you that the good of Kayı is
Ertuğrul Gazi!

119
00:17:00,040 --> 00:17:03,940
Right now, my father is on his death bed!

120
00:17:03,960 --> 00:17:08,740
For this, Kayı needs a new Bey.
And that Bey will be chosen tomorrow!

121
00:17:08,740 --> 00:17:13,040
Don' tell me you and uncle talked about
his with the other Beys!

122
00:17:15,579 --> 00:17:20,500
You want to become the new Bey while
Osman is not here, huh?

123
00:17:20,960 --> 00:17:22,740
Choose your words wisely, brother.

124
00:17:24,680 --> 00:17:26,350
I'm doing what's best for our Tent.

125
00:17:26,350 --> 00:17:27,980
No, you are not!

126
00:17:30,940 --> 00:17:32,460
You are only making it worse!

127
00:17:34,500 --> 00:17:36,620
You are going to bring the end of our
Tent!

128
00:17:48,020 --> 00:17:50,040
Don't you ever try this again, brother.

129
00:17:53,660 --> 00:17:54,760
As you wish, Savcı.

130
00:17:57,420 --> 00:17:58,620
As you wish, brother.

131
00:18:01,800 --> 00:18:03,680
Know that I'm watching you.

132
00:18:04,740 --> 00:18:08,000
I'm both watching you and Osman!

133
00:18:09,360 --> 00:18:15,880
I will make you remember that you have a
brother if you keep fighting like this.

134
00:18:18,880 --> 00:18:20,720
You can't imagine what I will do.

135
00:18:36,820 --> 00:18:38,240
Geyhatu.

136
00:18:48,840 --> 00:18:49,920
Geyhatu?

137
00:18:51,740 --> 00:18:56,520
While Geyhatu is alive, we can't rest,
Osman.

138
00:18:56,520 --> 00:18:58,940
Yalvak Arslan.

139
00:18:59,440 --> 00:19:03,400
Did you really try to kill me and my
brother in order to kill Geyhatu?

140
00:19:04,760 --> 00:19:06,800
Don't expect me to believe that.

141
00:19:09,300 --> 00:19:13,200
I had other causes as well but they were
no good.

142
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:20,360
I wanted to establish that state which the
Turks have been waiting for years.

143
00:19:21,360 --> 00:19:26,060
And I thought you were an obstacle for
this cause of mine.

144
00:19:31,080 --> 00:19:34,680
What changed now?

145
00:19:36,520 --> 00:19:38,060
Now, Osman...

146
00:19:41,560 --> 00:19:45,690
... maybe you will lay the foundations of
that very state...

147
00:19:45,690 --> 00:19:49,200
... which the Turks waiting for years.

148
00:19:57,040 --> 00:19:59,700
And the biggest obstacle before that
state...

149
00:20:05,920 --> 00:20:07,140
... is me.

150
00:20:29,160 --> 00:20:30,660
Your wound is too deep.

151
00:20:30,660 --> 00:20:32,660
We need to go to Inegöl at once.

152
00:20:36,060 --> 00:20:37,160
No.

153
00:20:38,500 --> 00:20:40,520
I can't explain this to Nikola.

154
00:20:42,080 --> 00:20:43,480
We are going back.

155
00:20:43,500 --> 00:20:44,720
All of our men died.

156
00:20:44,720 --> 00:20:46,980
How can we fight against them like this?

157
00:20:59,620 --> 00:21:01,180
I said we are going back.

158
00:21:03,020 --> 00:21:04,560
We are going back.

159
00:21:46,960 --> 00:21:48,980
I can't see what's inside of your heart.

160
00:21:51,040 --> 00:21:55,060
If you really think that you changed...

161
00:22:00,660 --> 00:22:05,680
... I can't say that you did not.

162
00:22:16,660 --> 00:22:20,140
Losing hope from a muslim...

163
00:22:23,080 --> 00:22:24,980
... is not acceptable for a muslim.

164
00:22:34,380 --> 00:22:37,300
Osman. Geyhatu is getting stronger.

165
00:22:39,200 --> 00:22:42,800
He wants to take Tabriz from Ilkhanates.

166
00:22:44,120 --> 00:22:46,600
The Emperor is satisfied with Nikola.

167
00:22:46,600 --> 00:22:50,800
Even if he loses Kulacahisar, Emperor will
keep supporting him with new armies.

168
00:22:51,120 --> 00:22:55,420
What I'm trying to say is that Kayı is
losing time.

169
00:22:59,160 --> 00:23:03,940
When it comes to Çobanoğulları, before
the Mongols leave Anatolia...

170
00:23:07,220 --> 00:23:09,100
... they can't sustain themselves.

171
00:23:14,320 --> 00:23:16,620
Are you saying that...

172
00:23:20,220 --> 00:23:21,680
... you want to be unified?

173
00:23:24,600 --> 00:23:26,720
Yes, indeed.

174
00:23:27,780 --> 00:23:30,260
These lands can't take this rivalry
anymore.

175
00:23:31,120 --> 00:23:34,840
Just like you said, Çobanoğulları and Kayı
can't rule together...

176
00:23:35,700 --> 00:23:40,120
... but if we don't unify now, there will
be neither Çobanoğullari nor Kayı.

177
00:23:50,940 --> 00:23:52,320
Then...

178
00:23:55,380 --> 00:23:58,920
... you won't stand on my way ever again
and try to stop me!

179
00:24:01,740 --> 00:24:04,560
You also won't use my uncle and brother
against me...

180
00:24:07,140 --> 00:24:11,220
... so that all of our enemies and Geyhatu
will be destroyed.

181
00:24:15,700 --> 00:24:17,900
This is the only thing I want from you.

182
00:24:21,060 --> 00:24:23,120
No, Osman. No!

183
00:24:24,680 --> 00:24:27,180
Geyhatu must die as soon as possible.

184
00:24:27,760 --> 00:24:33,360
Or else, both Kayı and Çobanoğulları
will have no future.

185
00:25:21,560 --> 00:25:23,880
Kayı Alp.

186
00:25:29,400 --> 00:25:31,240
Kayı Alp.

187
00:25:34,880 --> 00:25:37,080
You have a name now.

188
00:25:38,000 --> 00:25:43,320
Kayı’s Bey Osman gave you this name.

189
00:25:45,000 --> 00:25:47,320
He called you Kayı’s future.

190
00:25:57,760 --> 00:26:02,840
I won’t abandon you.
I won’t leave you without a mother.

191
00:26:03,880 --> 00:26:06,040
I’ll live for you.

192
00:26:07,360 --> 00:26:12,160
You and the future of Kayı.

193
00:26:15,880 --> 00:26:18,920
When will the meating take place, Bey?

194
00:26:19,760 --> 00:26:23,720
It’s about time, Hatun. Be prepared.

195
00:26:25,520 --> 00:26:29,480
If Osman comes, there will be chaos.

196
00:26:30,120 --> 00:26:35,480
There’s a chance Selcan
will fan the flame.

197
00:26:35,880 --> 00:26:40,280
You find out what they do with Lena.

198
00:26:41,160 --> 00:26:46,280
It’s enough if you stop them
from slowing me down.

199
00:26:52,080 --> 00:26:59,680
Once Osman dies, both
Selcan and Bala will be exiled.

200
00:27:01,400 --> 00:27:05,440
Father! What are you saying?

201
00:27:33,520 --> 00:27:38,640
Aygül! Since when are you back here?

202
00:27:40,520 --> 00:27:42,080
Where were you?

203
00:27:43,480 --> 00:27:46,560
I had things to do.

204
00:27:48,080 --> 00:27:50,160
Why do you ask?

205
00:27:50,800 --> 00:27:57,560
Were you actually sleeping
or secretly listening to us?

206
00:28:11,560 --> 00:28:17,520
Were you talking about things
I shouldn’t hear in broad daylight?

207
00:28:19,800 --> 00:28:26,880
Aygül. How long will
you keep acting this rebellious?

208
00:28:27,900 --> 00:28:30,040
When will you remember
that I’m your father?

209
00:28:30,040 --> 00:28:32,920
Once you start acting like a father!

210
00:28:41,960 --> 00:28:46,000
Hit me, father!
Don’t be afraid!

211
00:28:49,880 --> 00:28:54,480
Go away before I do
something bad. Go!

212
00:29:02,480 --> 00:29:09,240
Come, son. Come.

213
00:29:11,560 --> 00:29:17,160
This is the treatment your
mother gets until you can hold a sword.

214
00:29:19,360 --> 00:29:21,800
Come.

215
00:29:42,880 --> 00:29:45,480
Do you hear that, Dündar Bey?

216
00:29:45,480 --> 00:29:50,440
She’s filling your
grandson with hatred already.

217
00:29:51,000 --> 00:29:54,240
All because of Osman.

218
00:29:55,040 --> 00:30:03,120
Osman took your son, then your
daughter, and eventually your grandson.

219
00:30:06,600 --> 00:30:11,200
What is necessary will be done, Hatun!
What else do you want?

220
00:30:11,200 --> 00:30:15,200
So that you don’t change
your mind, Dündar Bey.

221
00:30:16,200 --> 00:30:19,440
Because I won’t.

222
00:30:30,240 --> 00:30:31,880
I won’t.

223
00:30:33,480 --> 00:30:35,800
Tell me, come on.

224
00:30:38,520 --> 00:30:42,720
I’m afraid the trick we’re
playing with Osman will be revealed.

225
00:30:48,280 --> 00:30:53,920
Don’t worry. We won’t act
before Osman Bey comes here.

226
00:31:00,080 --> 00:31:02,880
Nikola wants to talk to me tomorrow.

227
00:31:07,520 --> 00:31:09,760
About what?

228
00:31:09,760 --> 00:31:12,760
If you allow me, I’ll go and find out.

229
00:31:20,880 --> 00:31:26,520
Of course, daughter. Go and
learn. You’ll tell us what he tells you.

230
00:31:27,800 --> 00:31:32,560
Of course. Then, If you’ll excuse me…

231
00:31:32,560 --> 00:31:34,160
Of course, daughter.

232
00:31:53,440 --> 00:31:54,800
Aygül?

233
00:31:55,800 --> 00:31:59,240
Savcı Bey and my father will
conduct a meeting of Beys.

234
00:32:00,880 --> 00:32:04,360
- What are you saying?
- How could they?

235
00:32:06,440 --> 00:32:08,360
Would Osman accept this?

236
00:32:08,360 --> 00:32:13,320
He wouldn’t. And neither will we.

237
00:32:13,320 --> 00:32:17,760
Let them try and see what happens.

238
00:32:49,040 --> 00:32:51,400
I’ll go to Geyhatu’s headquarters.

239
00:32:51,400 --> 00:32:55,080
I’m his Head Bey.
He won’t doubt me.

240
00:32:56,120 --> 00:32:58,400
Does this have to
take place tomorrow?

241
00:32:58,400 --> 00:33:04,320
Geyhatu wanted to poison him.
If he did, he’ll want to check it.

242
00:33:14,520 --> 00:33:19,440
If Argun Khan is dead, Geyhatu
will be the Ilkhanid Emperor.

243
00:33:19,440 --> 00:33:21,520
I need to prevent that.

244
00:33:21,520 --> 00:33:27,560
Otherwise Geyhatu and his soldiers
will destroy the Turks in Anatolia.

245
00:33:29,840 --> 00:33:31,920
I will kill him.

246
00:33:39,760 --> 00:33:44,920
Now, we have news for Nikola.

247
00:33:45,680 --> 00:33:47,840
Should we leave?

248
00:33:48,640 --> 00:33:55,720
No. I want to listen to
the rest of their plan.

249
00:33:56,760 --> 00:34:01,760
I’ll attack Geyhatu’s
base with the rest of my Alps.

250
00:34:04,560 --> 00:34:07,800
Will this have the
same fate as the İnegöl Conquest?

251
00:34:08,040 --> 00:34:12,400
If Geyhatu survives,
none of us will enter İnegöl.

252
00:34:34,320 --> 00:34:38,239
If you say that you swore to give up…

253
00:34:38,239 --> 00:34:40,639
… that time’s running out…

254
00:34:42,320 --> 00:34:48,360
… and you walk on the path of faith…

255
00:34:52,840 --> 00:34:56,320
… then I won’t leave you
alone, Yavlak Arslan.

256
00:34:57,240 --> 00:35:02,480
After all the things I’ve done to you…

257
00:35:02,480 --> 00:35:04,880
You’re a brave man, Osman.

258
00:35:07,360 --> 00:35:09,400
Those were settled up with.

259
00:35:11,560 --> 00:35:17,320
You didn’t leave us alone.
So we won’t leave you alone.

260
00:35:22,760 --> 00:35:25,800
It was in our destiny
to fight side by side.

261
00:35:32,720 --> 00:35:34,800
Let’s go.

262
00:35:39,040 --> 00:35:42,680
Let’s get that cruel Geyhatu’s head.

263
00:35:42,680 --> 00:35:44,480
Are we friends?

264
00:35:44,480 --> 00:35:47,720
Until the Turk’s enemies give up.

265
00:35:47,720 --> 00:35:49,240
Praise be!

266
00:36:00,600 --> 00:36:03,160
I’ve heard enough.

267
00:36:03,160 --> 00:36:05,520
Let’s go.

268
00:36:21,960 --> 00:36:24,760
Savcı Bey is here!

269
00:37:03,440 --> 00:37:06,400
Peace be with you, Bamsı Bey.

270
00:37:06,400 --> 00:37:10,400
Peace be with you too, son.

271
00:37:10,400 --> 00:37:19,160
I was just sitting around the fire,
looking for a man to chat with. Here.

272
00:37:31,520 --> 00:37:37,560
If we keep conquering these
castles, we’ll get used to sitting here.

273
00:37:40,040 --> 00:37:42,640
What do you say, Bamsı Bey?

274
00:37:43,760 --> 00:37:53,560
Will be dead by then, son.
You’ll be sitting in castles then.

275
00:37:54,280 --> 00:37:58,480
Once my Osman comes,
I’ll return it anyway.

276
00:37:58,480 --> 00:38:09,280
Son, we’re old. If I’m going to die,
I want to die on a horse.

277
00:38:09,280 --> 00:38:13,160
- May Allah give you a long life.
- Thank you, son.

278
00:38:19,080 --> 00:38:22,240
You’re probably aware of
the situation, Bamsı Bey.

279
00:38:24,360 --> 00:38:30,400
My father may never
leave that bed again.

280
00:38:31,320 --> 00:38:34,640
We’ll have to choose a Bey eventually.

281
00:38:35,440 --> 00:38:39,520
We’ll face each other
with Osman eventually.

282
00:38:41,480 --> 00:38:45,880
He doesn’t hide his intentions.
From now on, neither will I.

283
00:38:47,400 --> 00:38:49,840
I want to be the Bey of Kayı.

284
00:38:52,120 --> 00:38:57,360
Of course you do, son.
You’re entitled to it.

285
00:38:58,400 --> 00:39:04,080
You know that Kayı Beys want
peace and choose me over Osman.

286
00:39:04,080 --> 00:39:09,760
Look son, no one knows that.

287
00:39:09,760 --> 00:39:11,920
I want something from you.

288
00:39:11,920 --> 00:39:13,880
What is it, son?

289
00:39:13,880 --> 00:39:22,240
If I become the Bey and
Osman doesn’t accept it…

290
00:39:22,240 --> 00:39:24,360
… stop him.

291
00:39:25,760 --> 00:39:29,240
How will I do that, son.

292
00:39:30,080 --> 00:39:32,440
Standing in his way will do.

293
00:39:34,320 --> 00:39:39,640
Standing in his way…
of Osman…

294
00:39:44,920 --> 00:39:54,040
What If I tell Osman not to accept…

295
00:39:54,400 --> 00:40:00,880
… those who move with the with
the words of potters and merchants…

296
00:40:00,880 --> 00:40:03,560
… as your Bey? What will you do then?

297
00:40:04,200 --> 00:40:07,760
Then, you will have
fanned the flame.

298
00:40:29,680 --> 00:40:33,800
Is that so, Bamsı Bey?

299
00:40:45,920 --> 00:40:52,600
Savcı Bey.
When will we make that decision?

300
00:40:52,600 --> 00:40:55,560
- Soon.
- How soon?

301
00:40:58,560 --> 00:41:02,000
- Very soon.
- Today?

302
00:41:04,080 --> 00:41:06,240
Is it today?

303
00:41:37,000 --> 00:41:40,040
[Bismillahirrahmanirrahim] In the name of Allah, the merciful and the compassionate.

304
00:41:40,560 --> 00:41:43,240
May it cure you, my Bey.

305
00:41:49,880 --> 00:41:57,560
So, they’ll conduct a
meeting and choose a Bey tomorrow.

306
00:42:01,640 --> 00:42:05,160
They buried me already.

307
00:42:05,160 --> 00:42:07,520
How could they, my Bey?

308
00:42:07,520 --> 00:42:12,520
They did.

309
00:42:16,720 --> 00:42:19,360
What will you do, my Bey?

310
00:42:22,520 --> 00:42:26,480
Listen to me carefully.

311
00:42:55,960 --> 00:42:58,640
I recognise this walk.

312
00:42:58,960 --> 00:43:02,280
This isn't the walk
of a victorious soldier!

313
00:43:08,040 --> 00:43:13,440
You couldn’t kill Osman, it seems.
What about the other duty?

314
00:43:17,440 --> 00:43:22,120
I see. Cerkutay is still alive.

315
00:43:24,160 --> 00:43:28,520
What did you even do, Flatyus?
What was your success?

316
00:43:29,840 --> 00:43:34,000
Osman caught Yavlak Arslan.
And I took Osman by surprise.

317
00:43:34,000 --> 00:43:35,360
And?

318
00:43:35,360 --> 00:43:38,600
We fought.
I made Osman drop his sword.

319
00:43:38,600 --> 00:43:40,400
As I was finishing him…

320
00:43:40,400 --> 00:43:43,000
And then, Flatyus?

321
00:43:43,000 --> 00:43:47,480
Yavlak Arslan interrupted.
He saved Osman and they teamed up.

322
00:43:47,480 --> 00:43:49,400
We were between two groups.

323
00:43:49,400 --> 00:43:51,400
What?

324
00:43:55,920 --> 00:43:59,600
Yavlak Arslan and
Osman teamed up?

325
00:44:01,440 --> 00:44:05,840
What are they up to?
What kind of a move is this?

326
00:44:06,920 --> 00:44:10,880
If you allow me, I shall tell
you what they are up to, Nikola.

327
00:44:10,880 --> 00:44:15,080
While I was unconscious,
my men took me away.

328
00:44:15,960 --> 00:44:20,400
I returned once I was
conscious again. I listened to them.

329
00:44:20,400 --> 00:44:22,360
Osman and Yavlak Arslan...

330
00:44:22,440 --> 00:44:24,640
... will kill Geyhatu.

331
00:44:31,560 --> 00:44:34,480
They might even be on the way now.

332
00:44:35,000 --> 00:44:39,320
They will kill Geyhatu.
They must be out of their minds!

333
00:44:44,640 --> 00:44:47,440
Do you really think they'll do it?

334
00:44:51,240 --> 00:44:56,200
Is there any chance
that they could do it?

335
00:44:57,240 --> 00:45:02,600
- It is Osman, Nikola.
- Right. It's Osman.

336
00:45:03,280 --> 00:45:08,720
If he kills Geyhatu and
gets out of there alive...

337
00:45:11,920 --> 00:45:16,640
... that wouldn't be
good, Flatyus. Not good.

338
00:45:19,720 --> 00:45:23,600
I'll go and tell Geyhatu this myself.

339
00:45:23,600 --> 00:45:28,160
By the way, we were going to
meet our spy in the Kayı Tent tomorrow.

340
00:45:28,160 --> 00:45:32,080
You'll meet me in
the forest before I meet her.

341
00:45:32,080 --> 00:45:35,080
I might give you new orders
based on Geyhatu's response.

342
00:45:35,080 --> 00:45:37,000
Okay, Nikola.

343
00:45:39,160 --> 00:45:44,080
Don't be sad, Flatyus.
This isn't your fault.

344
00:45:44,920 --> 00:45:48,680
You couldn't know that
Yavlak would do such a thing.

345
00:45:50,320 --> 00:45:54,200
Make them take care of your wound
and rest.

346
00:46:07,760 --> 00:46:11,560
Yavlak Arslan and Osman.

347
00:46:14,680 --> 00:46:16,800
Who could have guessed?

348
00:46:37,640 --> 00:46:39,400
What will we do?

349
00:46:39,400 --> 00:46:44,560
Once she gets away, you'll follow her.
I don't trust her.

350
00:46:45,120 --> 00:46:47,000
What will you do, Bala?

351
00:46:48,000 --> 00:46:50,720
We shouldn't leave the Tent to them.

352
00:46:50,720 --> 00:46:53,280
I'll stay here. You should go.

353
00:46:53,280 --> 00:46:55,280
Okay.

354
00:47:30,400 --> 00:47:33,640
Horse heart...

355
00:47:33,640 --> 00:47:36,920
Horse milk...

356
00:47:38,480 --> 00:47:41,440
Horse tongue...
Horse...

357
00:47:43,480 --> 00:47:47,320
Don't you eat things like lambs or cows?

358
00:47:47,320 --> 00:47:58,160
Mongols don't carry anything that
they can't use as a weapon.

359
00:48:01,840 --> 00:48:10,280
Those who go to war with lambs
and cows go slowly.

360
00:48:14,120 --> 00:48:17,760
Talk. Why did you come?

361
00:48:19,800 --> 00:48:23,640
I have some news
I think you'd like, Geyhatu.

362
00:48:24,080 --> 00:48:25,520
Talk.

363
00:48:25,520 --> 00:48:27,320
Osman.

364
00:48:29,320 --> 00:48:31,960
He ambushed Yavlak Arslan.

365
00:48:34,960 --> 00:48:39,640
My man attacked Osman
to save Yavlak Arslan.

366
00:48:40,320 --> 00:48:46,880
To save Yavlak Arslan...

367
00:48:47,640 --> 00:48:54,080
And Yavlak Arslan backstabbed
my man to save Osman, Geyhatu.

368
00:48:58,120 --> 00:49:04,280
Yavlak Arslan(Lion)
is such a strange lion.

369
00:49:05,480 --> 00:49:08,600
He's indeed a strange man.

370
00:49:08,600 --> 00:49:12,880
Möngke. Your son Möngke, Geyhatu.

371
00:49:12,880 --> 00:49:17,320
Do you know who he
teamed up with to kill you?

372
00:49:19,400 --> 00:49:21,480
Yavlak Arslan!

373
00:49:23,360 --> 00:49:29,360
Now, they teamed up with Osman.
They're coming for you, Geyhatu.

374
00:49:29,360 --> 00:49:34,800
Small men are very ambitious.

375
00:49:35,760 --> 00:49:45,480
Osman and Yavlak Arslan will come.
Geyhatu will make soup from their skins!

376
00:49:48,280 --> 00:49:50,120
I like soups!

377
00:49:50,800 --> 00:49:55,800
I want to help out.
May I kill a couple of Turks?

378
00:49:56,440 --> 00:50:02,200
Let's write a letter to Kayıs.

379
00:50:02,520 --> 00:50:06,960
- Our little Lord will take it to them.
- I'm honoured. What will it say?

380
00:50:06,960 --> 00:50:14,680
You'll hear while we write it.
Now, leave.

381
00:50:27,720 --> 00:50:36,400
Little Lord told me a lie and a truth.

382
00:50:37,960 --> 00:50:43,560
His men didn't want to save Yavlak.

383
00:50:43,560 --> 00:50:46,840
He wanted to kill Osman.

384
00:50:47,400 --> 00:50:55,680
These fools allied Osman and Yavlak.

385
00:50:55,680 --> 00:51:00,240
Now, they're coming here.

386
00:51:01,720 --> 00:51:06,600
I'll turn both of them into soup!

387
00:51:54,120 --> 00:51:58,240
- Don't disturb me while I'm eating, Kongar.
- Don't call me Kongar!

388
00:52:05,880 --> 00:52:12,240
I'll skin all you Mongols alive!

389
00:52:12,920 --> 00:52:16,720
I know that you want to die, Kongar.

390
00:52:19,360 --> 00:52:22,720
But don't expect it from me.

391
00:52:24,720 --> 00:52:30,480
If you call me Kongar again,
you'll have to kill me.

392
00:52:37,040 --> 00:52:40,520
We used to call you that.
Kongar.

393
00:52:41,880 --> 00:52:43,800
Göktuğ!

394
00:52:45,320 --> 00:52:50,040
Göktuğ, what are you doing, brother?
Our Bey is looking!

395
00:53:51,320 --> 00:53:57,040
We place Alps on this flank
and this flank.

396
00:53:59,480 --> 00:54:01,080
Then...

397
00:54:09,669 --> 00:54:13,079
You and I are going to get in
Geyhatu's tent.

398
00:54:19,707 --> 00:54:22,047
We are going to take Cerkutay with us.

399
00:54:26,560 --> 00:54:30,910
My Osman, I am okay to be martyres
with you, but...

400
00:54:31,953 --> 00:54:36,103
we can't even get near of that
tent.

401
00:54:37,347 --> 00:54:43,067
Yavlak Arslan, do you know how I get into
Kulucahisar all one?

402
00:54:44,733 --> 00:54:47,143
I wonder how.

403
00:54:47,878 --> 00:54:49,858
As a captive.

404
00:54:51,635 --> 00:54:55,845
I knew they'd take me to Nicola
when they captured me.

405
00:54:55,899 --> 00:54:59,829
- And that was what they did!
- Are you going to hand yourself in?

406
00:55:01,224 --> 00:55:02,914
Yes.

407
00:55:03,441 --> 00:55:05,091
I will.

408
00:55:08,964 --> 00:55:11,914
But this time I'll hand myself in you.

409
00:55:16,737 --> 00:55:18,637
In me?

410
00:56:04,147 --> 00:56:06,547
- There is news, Nicola.
- About what?

411
00:56:07,693 --> 00:56:11,913
- About Kayıs.
- What are these Kayıs after, Vladius?

412
00:56:12,256 --> 00:56:16,576
- They are meeting to choose a Bey.
- Choosing a Bey?

413
00:56:17,599 --> 00:56:19,599
While Osman is gone.

414
00:56:21,933 --> 00:56:28,283
What happens if they choose a
Bey while Osman is not there, Vladius?

415
00:56:28,756 --> 00:56:33,387
Osman and his Alps will deny it, Nicola.

416
00:56:33,387 --> 00:56:34,987
That's right.

417
00:56:35,421 --> 00:56:40,621
Geyhatu will kill Osman. Kayıs will be
messed up on choosing a new Bey..

418
00:56:42,038 --> 00:56:45,588
And we will take what we've lost
back.

419
00:56:48,678 --> 00:56:51,328
Are you a brave man, Vladius?

420
00:56:53,957 --> 00:56:56,459
You say, Nicola.
Am I?

421
00:56:56,459 --> 00:57:01,999
You are a man who can dare to go to
Kayı tribe all alone.

422
00:57:03,584 --> 00:57:08,884
Is there anything else I should do
other than letting them kill me?

423
00:57:08,948 --> 00:57:11,728
There is. There is.

424
00:57:11,802 --> 00:57:18,732
You will go to Kayı Tribe. You'll inform
Dündar and Savcı Bey that we declare war.

425
00:57:19,355 --> 00:57:22,685
Then they are going to kill me, right?

426
00:57:22,920 --> 00:57:26,930
Vladius, didn't you want to die?

427
00:57:28,130 --> 00:57:30,900
You know I am going to go there, Nicola.

428
00:57:31,562 --> 00:57:35,182
I just have to make sure that this
is right for Rome.

429
00:57:41,714 --> 00:57:44,924
A letter from Geyhatu to Kayıs.

430
00:57:46,647 --> 00:57:50,197
This is right for Rome, Vladius.

431
00:57:54,620 --> 00:57:58,200
- What does this say, Nicola?
- Beautiful things.

432
00:57:58,295 --> 00:58:02,175
I like beautiful things, Vladius.
I'll tell you about it.

433
00:58:02,249 --> 00:58:07,919
But before going to Kayı tribe,
take those clothes off.

434
00:58:08,513 --> 00:58:12,803
Wear something decent to
represent Rome.

435
00:58:14,851 --> 00:58:17,501
Let's see what Targun has done.

436
00:58:17,541 --> 00:58:19,451
Targun.

437
00:58:31,794 --> 00:58:36,704
What would you do if you were Osman...

438
00:58:36,758 --> 00:58:42,068
and people gathered a meeting to choose
a new Bey, Lena?

439
00:58:42,904 --> 00:58:46,314
I'd be aware that I wouldn't be able to
live here anymore.

440
00:58:46,343 --> 00:58:48,743
So I'd do anything to prevent this from
happening.

441
00:58:50,037 --> 00:58:52,847
So he'll do his best.

442
00:58:53,391 --> 00:58:56,771
But the question is...

443
00:58:58,798 --> 00:59:01,148
what can he do?

444
00:59:15,785 --> 00:59:19,785
What's it, Selcen Hatun?
Are you lost?

445
00:59:21,354 --> 00:59:26,004
Or are you searching someone to
insult?

446
00:59:26,006 --> 00:59:27,556
No.

447
00:59:27,878 --> 00:59:32,558
I've heard that Dündar and Savcı Beys
arranging a meeting.

448
00:59:34,121 --> 00:59:36,331
Their Hatuns were absent.

449
00:59:37,128 --> 00:59:40,608
So I wondered you.

450
00:59:44,619 --> 00:59:48,159
Thank you, thank you.

451
00:59:48,745 --> 00:59:53,845
We don't need to do anything
for now.

452
00:59:55,970 --> 01:00:00,960
If you don't do something stupid...

453
01:00:01,689 --> 01:00:04,019
we won't have any problem.

454
01:00:07,126 --> 01:00:11,846
What can I say?
This is what I am.

455
01:00:11,924 --> 01:00:15,224
You can't predict what I am going to do.

456
01:00:15,931 --> 01:00:20,891
But if there is a meeting being aranged
while my Osman is absent...

457
01:00:21,050 --> 01:00:24,550
I feel I must do something.

458
01:00:27,964 --> 01:00:30,124
Selcan Hatun.

459
01:00:31,158 --> 01:00:33,788
Aren't you afraid that...

460
01:00:35,443 --> 01:00:40,963
something bad may happen to you
while Osman is not here to protect you?

461
01:00:43,053 --> 01:00:45,243
May Allah prevent.

462
01:00:46,669 --> 01:00:49,279
If Osman Bey's not here, I am here.

463
01:00:52,596 --> 01:00:55,766
Who can do something bad to Selcen Hatun?

464
01:01:04,627 --> 01:01:07,737
Don't push your luck, Bala.

465
01:01:15,050 --> 01:01:17,920
So you say this is a new era, huh?

466
01:01:22,732 --> 01:01:28,352
You think it'll be too late when
my Osman is back.

467
01:01:31,881 --> 01:01:37,251
Okay then, I'll think of something
before my Osman arrives in here.

468
01:01:51,493 --> 01:01:55,753
You turned Dündar and Savcı Bey against
my Osman.

469
01:01:57,440 --> 01:02:01,770
You send the old hunter
to hunt a lion.

470
01:02:03,759 --> 01:02:08,399
You troubled your Beys.

471
01:02:10,195 --> 01:02:17,606
You couldn't see what a lion
is capable of...

472
01:02:17,606 --> 01:02:22,196
when someone try to hunt him down.

473
01:02:22,889 --> 01:02:29,779
I hope the best end for you.

474
01:02:30,819 --> 01:02:32,749
Open the doors!

475
01:02:59,047 --> 01:03:02,297
Boran, Göktuğ.

476
01:03:04,507 --> 01:03:07,797
- Hide where I told you to.
- Eyvallah (okay) my Bey.

477
01:03:08,078 --> 01:03:09,418
Eyvallah my Bey.

478
01:03:12,548 --> 01:03:18,278
Gence Bey, you are one of us now.
Take a good care of yourself.

479
01:03:18,366 --> 01:03:23,136
Don't worry, Osman Bey.
We'll fight with the sign of yours.

480
01:03:23,555 --> 01:03:25,135
Eyvallah (thank you).

481
01:03:27,458 --> 01:03:28,908
Yavlak Arslan.

482
01:03:31,628 --> 01:03:33,588
Let's go.

483
01:03:33,941 --> 01:03:36,171
May our holy war be blessed.

484
01:03:45,302 --> 01:03:47,162
Yes.

485
01:04:03,987 --> 01:04:08,797
Targun, the power that infiltrated into
Kayı tribe.

486
01:04:10,342 --> 01:04:12,542
Is Osman dead?

487
01:04:12,911 --> 01:04:17,321
- It's not that easy, Nicola.
- No, no, you are right.

488
01:04:17,918 --> 01:04:21,138
Osman hasn't ever been a piece of cake.

489
01:04:22,014 --> 01:04:26,714
Let's go there and kill all of them!
We can get rid of Nicola fast!

490
01:04:26,858 --> 01:04:29,788
Wait, Aygül!
Wait!

491
01:04:31,105 --> 01:04:34,295
Check it.
They are crowded.

492
01:04:34,484 --> 01:04:39,804
Would Osman Bey let his cousin die
because of that dog?

493
01:04:40,264 --> 01:04:43,434
Let's get the information and
go back.

494
01:04:45,284 --> 01:04:49,654
This is not a simple infidel.
This is a big infidel.

495
01:04:51,613 --> 01:04:57,443
I can just take his life and
be martyred.

496
01:04:57,484 --> 01:05:05,444
Aygül, one thousand Byzantine
soldiers don't worth you.

497
01:05:07,879 --> 01:05:12,339
Now our mission is to learn
what is going on here.

498
01:05:15,082 --> 01:05:16,892
Eyvallah (okay) Gonca.

499
01:05:18,110 --> 01:05:19,912
Let's wait and see.

500
01:05:19,912 --> 01:05:24,012
Enough, Nicola!
What do you want from me?

501
01:05:25,116 --> 01:05:27,956
I want the congratulate you at first.

502
01:05:28,009 --> 01:05:35,072
You are getting married to Osman. I would
wish you kids, little Osmans, but...

503
01:05:35,072 --> 01:05:37,832
this would not be good for me.

504
01:05:38,540 --> 01:05:41,310
Yes, we are getting married.

505
01:05:42,121 --> 01:05:44,931
You did your job well, obviously.

506
01:05:45,605 --> 01:05:48,225
This was faster then I expected.

507
01:05:49,680 --> 01:05:51,724
They are coming here, Aygül.

508
01:05:51,724 --> 01:05:54,237
We must kill them.
They are two.

509
01:05:54,237 --> 01:05:56,717
- One can shout.
- We silence them.

510
01:05:56,796 --> 01:06:00,166
- One for you, one for me.
- Agreed.

511
01:06:04,411 --> 01:06:07,401
Osman didn't get suspicious of you.

512
01:06:07,862 --> 01:06:10,179
He did, surely.

513
01:06:10,179 --> 01:06:11,739
So?

514
01:06:12,192 --> 01:06:14,932
And I told him everything.

515
01:06:16,737 --> 01:06:21,317
I told him that you abducted my father
and that was why I had to help you.

516
01:06:24,752 --> 01:06:30,362
Good girl. You are beyond the
expectations! Good my little devil!

517
01:06:35,731 --> 01:06:38,231
When are you going to free my father?

518
01:06:38,890 --> 01:06:42,130
Targun, Targun, Targun!

519
01:06:46,786 --> 01:06:48,296
This is not gold.

520
01:06:50,967 --> 01:06:52,487
This is poison.

521
01:06:53,543 --> 01:06:58,453
You are going to poison each Bey
in Kayı tribe, but..

522
01:06:58,473 --> 01:07:00,663
but...

523
01:07:02,711 --> 01:07:06,801
Do it all together, I don't want to work
on them one by one.

524
01:07:06,801 --> 01:07:09,984
You can handle it, don't give me
that look.

525
01:07:09,984 --> 01:07:14,707
Why? Because Targun doesn't want her
father to die.

526
01:07:14,707 --> 01:07:16,637
Isn't that right?

527
01:07:17,169 --> 01:07:19,449
Right, Targun?

528
01:07:20,317 --> 01:07:21,857
It's right.

529
01:08:00,254 --> 01:08:02,624
We shared them, Aygül!

530
01:08:02,633 --> 01:08:04,653
I couldn't stop myself.

531
01:08:14,120 --> 01:08:15,680
Come on Aygül.

532
01:08:29,513 --> 01:08:31,593
Nicola is gone.

533
01:08:33,105 --> 01:08:35,305
What is she doing there?

534
01:08:52,042 --> 01:08:54,862
How can I do this to them?

535
01:09:04,531 --> 01:09:07,171
I follow your path, my father.

536
01:09:07,803 --> 01:09:10,353
I am striving for Kayı's future.

537
01:09:14,646 --> 01:09:17,466
My heart is crying, but...

538
01:09:18,353 --> 01:09:20,783
there is nothing left to do.

539
01:09:25,423 --> 01:09:27,133
Brother...

540
01:09:27,622 --> 01:09:31,912
if you hear us, you should know that...

541
01:09:32,365 --> 01:09:39,445
our objective is good. We are doing this
to make sure that your efforts...

542
01:09:40,030 --> 01:09:42,680
don't be wasted.

543
01:09:43,859 --> 01:09:49,839
Dündar Bey, it is not good to
arrange a meeting...

544
01:09:50,382 --> 01:09:55,502
before Osman Bey comes here.

545
01:09:56,226 --> 01:10:03,176
If Ertuğrul Bey wakes up and hears all
about this...

546
01:10:05,095 --> 01:10:08,485
he won't give his blessings to you.

547
01:10:08,572 --> 01:10:12,372
You are talking like you know
my father better than me, Abdurrahman Bey.

548
01:10:14,332 --> 01:10:15,962
Son.

549
01:10:18,970 --> 01:10:24,340
I spend my whole life fighting with
Eruğrul Bey back to back.

550
01:10:25,703 --> 01:10:31,283
We went to battlefield with my Bey
while you were not born.

551
01:10:31,743 --> 01:10:35,453
Of course I know about him.

552
01:10:39,368 --> 01:10:42,878
Welcome, Beys.

553
01:10:44,283 --> 01:10:48,413
Nephew, let's go in.

554
01:10:49,523 --> 01:10:51,383
Let's go uncle.

555
01:11:22,633 --> 01:11:27,493
My Bey, wake up. Wake up.

556
01:11:28,173 --> 01:11:31,971
Wake up and prevent this
disaster from happening.

557
01:11:32,214 --> 01:11:36,244
Otherwise, it's going to be
bad.

558
01:11:39,599 --> 01:11:42,255
Bismillahirrahmanirrahim.
(in the name of allah the merciful the compassionate)

559
01:11:42,255 --> 01:11:51,375
With the 99 name of Allah, who is the
most powerful one, to whom we pray.

560
01:11:59,875 --> 01:12:01,545
My Beys...

561
01:12:15,240 --> 01:12:19,050
Welcome, Beys, Aghas.

562
01:12:27,326 --> 01:12:29,476
Thanks.

563
01:12:34,109 --> 01:12:37,979
Welcome to my Ertuğrul Bey's tent.

564
01:12:44,723 --> 01:12:46,983
What is this about, Selcen Hatun?

565
01:12:50,663 --> 01:12:52,703
Is there something important?

566
01:12:53,195 --> 01:12:56,715
Yes there is something important.

567
01:12:57,608 --> 01:12:59,408
Tell us.

568
01:13:00,251 --> 01:13:03,551
I've heard that you are choosing a Bey.

569
01:13:04,343 --> 01:13:07,423
Then yes, there is something important.

570
01:13:07,719 --> 01:13:13,119
But tell me, Dündar. How are you going to
choose that Bey while my Osman is absent?

571
01:13:21,942 --> 01:13:27,632
Aunt, you know the tradition.
Women are not allowed in meetings.

572
01:13:28,059 --> 01:13:32,992
Yes, I know the tradition.
I also know that...

573
01:13:32,992 --> 01:13:36,192
my Ertuğrul Bey is still alive.

574
01:13:44,132 --> 01:13:50,002
He is alive but he is not healthy
enough to reign...

575
01:13:50,226 --> 01:13:52,306
Don't talk too much Dündar!

576
01:13:53,625 --> 01:13:57,795
I know the tradition.
I am asking to you...

577
01:13:57,881 --> 01:14:01,971
isn't each son of Bey the heir of
Beyship?

578
01:14:14,545 --> 01:14:21,375
What does this mean? You gather a meeting
in a hurry while Osman is away for duty.

579
01:14:22,160 --> 01:14:25,630
Aunt, your opinions aren't valid here.

580
01:14:26,874 --> 01:14:30,794
Selcan Hatun is one of the notable ones
in our community.

581
01:14:31,195 --> 01:14:34,165
She has right to speak.

582
01:14:39,564 --> 01:14:43,904
Yes, I do of course.

583
01:14:45,959 --> 01:14:49,979
And I stand up for Osman Bey.

584
01:14:53,199 --> 01:14:57,319
If Osman Bey is absent, I am here for him.

585
01:15:29,158 --> 01:15:30,588
Walk!

586
01:15:43,909 --> 01:15:49,199
- I brough the traitors for Geyhatu.
- Geyhatu wants to see them now!

587
01:15:56,570 --> 01:15:58,400
Walk!

588
01:15:59,280 --> 01:16:01,410
Make room for me Gündüz.

589
01:16:02,935 --> 01:16:05,215
Here I am!

590
01:16:08,129 --> 01:16:13,149
Is there anyone who can
throw me out?

591
01:16:24,407 --> 01:16:26,347
Selcan Aunt.

592
01:16:28,592 --> 01:16:31,792
Don't make me use force.

593
01:16:33,303 --> 01:16:36,863
You can't touch me Dündar.

594
01:16:56,747 --> 01:16:59,587
Hey, Dündar Bey, Hey.

595
01:17:02,420 --> 01:17:05,200
Hey, Dündar Bey, Hey.

596
01:17:09,916 --> 01:17:13,646
Hey, Savcı Bey, Hey.

597
01:17:18,247 --> 01:17:23,267
Hey Kayı Beys, Hey.

598
01:17:23,873 --> 01:17:25,833
Kayı Beys...

599
01:17:27,183 --> 01:17:31,823
You can do anything!

600
01:17:31,844 --> 01:17:34,944
You are powerful enough for anything!

601
01:17:35,055 --> 01:17:37,095
Bamsı...

602
01:17:37,226 --> 01:17:40,676
But, but...

603
01:17:41,805 --> 01:17:45,385
do you know what you can't do?

604
01:17:50,703 --> 01:17:56,113
You can't touch Selcan Hatun.

605
01:18:04,637 --> 01:18:06,577
Bamsı...

606
01:18:10,275 --> 01:18:15,525
Ah Dündar Bey! You couldn't
throw that Selcan Hatun out!

607
01:18:17,494 --> 01:18:19,844
Now that Bamsı Bey is here...

608
01:18:20,965 --> 01:18:25,905
I call this meeting to end.

609
01:18:27,620 --> 01:18:31,721
Bamsı Bey's arrival is no good.
Things will get messed up.

610
01:18:31,721 --> 01:18:35,071
Savcı Bey was supposed to
convince Bamsı Bey.

611
01:18:36,336 --> 01:18:40,726
Come on, Hazal Hatun. Who can turn Bamsı
Bey against Osman Bey?

612
01:18:45,494 --> 01:18:48,524
Walk! Traitor!

613
01:18:50,766 --> 01:18:52,546
Walk!

614
01:18:52,819 --> 01:18:54,459
Walk!

615
01:19:00,137 --> 01:19:01,777
Walk!

616
01:19:06,471 --> 01:19:09,881
- Geyhatu will beat us down.
- Shut up! Walk!

617
01:19:10,566 --> 01:19:14,596
Let them talk.
These are their last words!

618
01:19:17,422 --> 01:19:23,633
Mongol's dog! I will kill you myself
as soon as I get out of here.

619
01:19:23,633 --> 01:19:28,183
Osman, look around.

620
01:19:28,790 --> 01:19:31,410
How can you stay alive out of here?

621
01:19:34,267 --> 01:19:36,477
Walk!

622
01:19:39,735 --> 01:19:41,635
Walk!

623
01:19:43,801 --> 01:19:45,561
Walk now!

624
01:19:53,427 --> 01:19:55,837
What is this about?

625
01:19:57,075 --> 01:19:59,715
What if Osman is here?

626
01:21:00,831 --> 01:21:07,151
''Heathen! Leave our lands!
Leave here, you heathen!''

627
01:21:07,335 --> 01:21:13,535
Stay calm, gentlemen. Stay calm.
I came alone. I'm unarmed.

628
01:21:14,160 --> 01:21:20,000
-I have important news for your bey.
-Unmount.

629
01:21:33,690 --> 01:21:36,210
Wait here.

630
01:22:00,895 --> 01:22:04,285
Baysungur, what's this fuss?

631
01:22:04,285 --> 01:22:10,085
Flatyos is here
He has important news.

632
01:22:10,108 --> 01:22:14,368
He should wait. We'll find out after
the meeting.

633
01:22:14,368 --> 01:22:21,258
No. We aren't in a hurry.
Let's see what he has to say.

634
01:22:24,055 --> 01:22:28,055
If had the courage to come here,
it must be important.

635
01:22:39,900 --> 01:22:43,370
Baysungur, bring him.

636
01:22:45,197 --> 01:22:49,197
Let him come and speak.

637
01:23:03,006 --> 01:23:07,506
Are you going to deceive us with peace
again?

638
01:23:07,856 --> 01:23:12,236
On contrary, I came to declare war.

639
01:23:25,400 --> 01:23:27,660
War?

640
01:23:31,061 --> 01:23:34,001
You want war?

641
01:23:35,316 --> 01:23:38,496
If you allow me...

642
01:23:42,480 --> 01:23:47,220
...I should convey Gethatu's letter.

643
01:23:47,493 --> 01:23:49,793
Geyhatu?

644
01:23:51,104 --> 01:23:54,384
Why does he intervene?

645
01:24:22,698 --> 01:24:24,448
Move!

646
01:25:38,961 --> 01:25:46,361
He gave Kulucahisar, Söğüt
and Karacahisar to Nikola.

647
01:25:53,196 --> 01:25:57,196
If we don't leave them in
three days...

648
01:25:58,186 --> 01:26:02,456
If you don't, there will be a war between
Geyhatu and the Kayı.

649
01:26:02,456 --> 01:26:07,566
Rome will stand with Geyhatu with
all its strenght.

650
01:26:09,545 --> 01:26:12,825
If needed, of course.

651
01:26:19,947 --> 01:26:24,757
And by the way, Argun Khan died.

652
01:26:25,686 --> 01:26:29,686
Geyhatu will be the ruler of
Ilkhaganete soon.

653
01:26:30,220 --> 01:26:34,950
So, you'll fight against the
empire of Ilkhaganate.

654
01:26:42,312 --> 01:26:49,942
Enough! Enough!
Be silent! Be silent!

655
01:26:52,373 --> 01:27:00,983
After we send him, we should dismiss the
election meeting and start a war meeting.

656
01:27:02,172 --> 01:27:10,202
And Osman will manage the war meeting.
He is the only one who can do it.

657
01:27:13,574 --> 01:27:17,574
-Osman?
-Yeah, Osman.

658
01:27:21,951 --> 01:27:25,951
-Osman, huh?
-Osman, yes. Yes, Osman, kid.

659
01:27:26,021 --> 01:27:32,431
Osman who I warned many times about this?
Osman who brought this upon us?

660
01:27:32,742 --> 01:27:37,842
Do you expect him to bring us victory
against Ilkhaganete?

661
01:27:38,303 --> 01:27:42,873
Will we fight with a country that has
a thousand warriors for each of ours?

662
01:27:42,873 --> 01:27:44,283
Yes!

663
01:27:44,863 --> 01:27:47,103
-Bamsı Bey!
-Savcı!

664
01:27:48,339 --> 01:27:51,679
Bamsı Bey.
Bamsı Bey.

665
01:27:53,037 --> 01:27:58,557
Savcı Bey, Bamsı Bey is our elder.

666
01:28:06,048 --> 01:28:09,248
You will fight.

667
01:28:17,946 --> 01:28:22,846
If we all going to die, I should skin him.
-My nephew!

668
01:28:27,654 --> 01:28:32,774
We don't hurt envoys.
Don't forget our traditions.

669
01:28:39,077 --> 01:28:43,077
Have you forgot that they stabbed me
on my back and tortured me.

670
01:28:54,532 --> 01:29:00,352
You said what you have to say.
Now leave here.

671
01:29:02,720 --> 01:29:06,480
Don't you wonder where Osman is?

672
01:29:12,883 --> 01:29:16,403
Tell me where Osman is.

673
01:29:17,291 --> 01:29:20,951
Osman allied Yavlak Arslan.

674
01:29:27,660 --> 01:29:33,520
-Tell me the truth. How do you know that?
-Yavlak Arslan saved Osman from my hands.

675
01:29:36,071 --> 01:29:40,071
And they are probably on their way to
Geyhatu's tents.

676
01:29:44,230 --> 01:29:49,550
-Why would Osman go there?
-If I know Osman well...

677
01:29:49,572 --> 01:29:53,572
...he is going there to stab
Geyhatu on his heart.

678
01:30:08,164 --> 01:30:14,144
Hazal Hatun, how can your brother
Yavlak Arslan form alliance with Osman?

679
01:30:15,852 --> 01:30:19,852
-I'm talking to you, Hazal Hatun.
-Enough!

680
01:30:19,852 --> 01:30:25,202
Hazal Hatun, Hazal Hatun. I hear you!
I'm not deaf!

681
01:30:36,313 --> 01:30:40,313
I brought you the traitors, Geyhatu.

682
01:31:14,984 --> 01:31:18,984
No one can deceive Geyhatu.

683
01:31:35,647 --> 01:31:41,067
Argun Khan died.
Argun Khan is no more.

684
01:31:44,402 --> 01:31:50,462
The great enemy is defeated.
The poison worked.

685
01:31:51,167 --> 01:31:57,237
Prepare the warriors.
I'm going to Tebriz.

686
01:31:57,237 --> 01:32:02,487
Geyhatu will sit on Argun Khan's throne.

687
01:32:02,487 --> 01:32:05,948
What will happen to Osman?

688
01:32:05,948 --> 01:32:10,528
Geyhatu will be the great khagan.

689
01:32:13,251 --> 01:32:17,251
You will kill the little beys.

690
01:32:17,999 --> 01:32:22,999
While he is on his way to
the throne in Tebriz, you'll die here.

691
01:32:24,571 --> 01:32:28,571
Just like Argun Khan.

692
01:32:49,210 --> 01:32:52,270
Think, beys.

693
01:32:53,770 --> 01:32:59,120
But don't forget.
You have three days.

694
01:33:38,660 --> 01:33:40,830
-Saltuk!
-Yes, my bey?

695
01:33:40,974 --> 01:33:44,444
Take him out.
Come on!

696
01:34:27,114 --> 01:34:31,644
There is still no sign.
Something is wrong.

697
01:34:35,902 --> 01:34:39,902
Brother, should we wait a little longer?

698
01:34:48,125 --> 01:34:50,425
Come on now!

699
01:35:13,322 --> 01:35:16,972
It seems that they are ambushed.

700
01:35:30,359 --> 01:35:35,369
-They are ambushed, come on!
-Unsheathe, brothers!

701
01:35:40,851 --> 01:35:47,321
Beys of Kayı!
The meeting is over.

702
01:35:53,749 --> 01:35:59,219
Now, pray Allah for Osman to return.

703
01:36:02,665 --> 01:36:08,265
And no one should do things
behind Osman.

704
01:37:31,090 --> 01:37:33,390
We are here, Osman Bey!

705
01:40:11,430 --> 01:40:14,690
Brotherhood of war doesn't
end that easily.

706
01:40:59,322 --> 01:41:01,892
Brothers!

707
01:41:03,557 --> 01:41:07,557
Victory belongs to those who believe!

708
01:41:07,616 --> 01:41:12,986
Allahu Akbar! Allahu Akbar!
Allahu Akbar!

709
01:41:15,400 --> 01:41:20,010
Geyhatu took his army and left.
And he set a trap for us.

710
01:41:20,010 --> 01:41:23,840
He'll return even stronger.

711
01:41:24,007 --> 01:41:28,007
Now, he'll return as the sultan
of Ilkhaganate.

712
01:41:28,133 --> 01:41:31,233
Let him come!

713
01:41:32,725 --> 01:41:36,895
So, Yavlak Arslan...

714
01:41:38,998 --> 01:41:45,338
...you fought well.
-I'm glad to witness your fighting.

715
01:41:55,989 --> 01:42:02,339
Flatyos, you'll leave these tents
safe and sound.

716
01:42:06,912 --> 01:42:12,332
Turkic tents are the lair of lions.

717
01:42:15,431 --> 01:42:19,431
Because even the unhonorable ones...

718
01:42:19,879 --> 01:42:22,839
...gets treated with honor.

719
01:42:23,827 --> 01:42:29,447
Tell the Rum lord Nikola,
we won't hand over...

720
01:42:29,447 --> 01:42:33,447
...Kulucahisar, Söğüt
or Karacahisar...

721
01:42:33,447 --> 01:42:36,987
...without a fight.

722
01:42:42,994 --> 01:42:49,174
Not Geyhatu, even Genghis Khan
if he wakes up from death...

723
01:42:49,374 --> 01:42:53,694
...can't ask us to accept that.

724
01:42:53,737 --> 01:42:58,617
Allahu Akbar! Allahu Akbar!
Allahu Akber!

725
01:43:01,402 --> 01:43:05,402
Mighty Allah is my witness that...

726
01:43:05,638 --> 01:43:09,638
...I've done everything I could...

727
01:43:10,853 --> 01:43:14,853
...to prevent a war coming
to our tents.

728
01:43:18,158 --> 01:43:26,658
To live in peace, to night fight
with neither the Mongols nor the Rums...

729
01:43:28,197 --> 01:43:32,197
...I even took the change of
getting called a craven.

730
01:43:32,731 --> 01:43:43,831
But, but,
if war is in our destiny...

731
01:43:44,577 --> 01:43:50,097
...either it's the enemy who brings it
or it's my brother, I'll fight!

732
01:43:55,249 --> 01:44:02,539
Neither I'll give you my brother Osman,
nor a crumble of land!

733
01:44:05,148 --> 01:44:09,148
We, we came to these lands...

734
01:44:09,326 --> 01:44:17,116
...and sacrificed our blood for these
lands. We aren't giving them back!

735
01:44:18,703 --> 01:44:25,113
We came to these lands to build a state!

736
01:44:26,324 --> 01:44:30,324
And we'll build that state!

737
01:44:30,556 --> 01:44:35,516
Long live Savcı Bey! Long live Savcı Bey!
Long live Savcı Bey! Long live Savcı Bey!

738
01:44:47,987 --> 01:44:49,887
Go on!

739
01:44:51,013 --> 01:44:53,213
Leave now.

740
01:46:01,569 --> 01:46:03,779
The door of penitence...

741
01:46:05,351 --> 01:46:08,741
...is it open for non-muslims too?

742
01:46:13,798 --> 01:46:16,018
Göktuğ.

743
01:46:20,249 --> 01:46:22,629
Inshallah.

744
01:46:29,187 --> 01:46:33,187
Inshallah you will forswear and
become muslim, Cerkutay.

745
01:46:53,706 --> 01:46:56,276
Inshallah.

746
01:47:10,741 --> 01:47:13,301
So, Yavlak Arslan...

747
01:47:13,919 --> 01:47:20,579
...what will you do?
-When Geyhatu returns as the khagan...

748
01:47:20,881 --> 01:47:25,031
...all the Çobanoğlu tribe will stand
against him with their swords.

749
01:47:30,258 --> 01:47:33,818
What will you do, Osman Bey?

750
01:47:46,628 --> 01:47:49,748
The disgraceful meeting has ended.

751
01:47:50,872 --> 01:47:53,952
The election of the bey is for tomorrow.

752
01:47:54,673 --> 01:47:58,673
The bad days are over,
the worse days are there to come.

753
01:48:07,015 --> 01:48:09,745
Tell us.
What does Nikola want?

754
01:48:10,049 --> 01:48:11,809
What does he want from you?

755
01:48:18,534 --> 01:48:20,444
He wants me to kill Osman Bey.

756
01:48:24,549 --> 01:48:26,529
You what?

757
01:48:28,853 --> 01:48:30,773
How will you kill him?

758
01:48:30,773 --> 01:48:31,683
Huh?

759
01:48:33,080 --> 01:48:35,360
It's Osman Bey's word.

760
01:48:35,532 --> 01:48:40,482
When we marry, Nikola will be happy and
he'll think that I'll kill Osman easily.

761
01:48:41,349 --> 01:48:42,349
However...

762
01:48:43,139 --> 01:48:47,139
Osman Bey knows that I won't
do such a thing.

763
01:48:48,246 --> 01:48:50,556
He knows that I just want to
save my father.

764
01:48:53,487 --> 01:48:55,007
Osman Bey...

765
01:48:55,447 --> 01:48:58,417
has done the right thing
by choosing you, Targun.

766
01:48:59,030 --> 01:49:01,620
However, I have to save
my father.

767
01:49:02,314 --> 01:49:07,784
Poison. You'll poison the Beys
in the Kayı tribe with this.

768
01:49:09,340 --> 01:49:13,340
Do it when they are all together.

769
01:49:13,760 --> 01:49:17,260
As Targun doesn't want her father
to die.

770
01:49:18,044 --> 01:49:20,414
I have to protect my father.

771
01:49:45,263 --> 01:49:47,303
Whether Osman or Yavlak Arslan...

772
01:49:47,467 --> 01:49:51,287
won't come out alive from Geyhatu's tribe.

773
01:49:52,156 --> 01:49:54,256
Ah, brother...

774
01:49:54,348 --> 01:49:56,668
his greed causes him trouble.

775
01:49:57,668 --> 01:49:59,588
We shouldn't make a choice.

776
01:49:59,805 --> 01:50:03,185
I'll declare my Beyship tomorrow.

777
01:50:12,441 --> 01:50:13,431
Nephew...

778
01:50:15,783 --> 01:50:19,783
If Osman is alive and becomes an
ally with Yavlak Arslan...

779
01:50:20,733 --> 01:50:22,433
he won't forgive you.

780
01:50:22,545 --> 01:50:27,345
Your Alps can't set against Osman's Alps.

781
01:50:28,232 --> 01:50:29,322
He comes and...

782
01:50:29,890 --> 01:50:32,560
takes Beyship.

783
01:50:33,516 --> 01:50:36,406
If the Beyship is taken, it
won't be given back.

784
01:50:36,487 --> 01:50:38,187
If Osman is alive...

785
01:50:39,033 --> 01:50:43,033
I'll take him to court...

786
01:50:43,629 --> 01:50:45,909
because of endangering Kayıs'
peace.

787
01:50:46,806 --> 01:50:49,846
What matters if he is an
ally with Yavlak Arslan?

788
01:50:50,613 --> 01:50:53,943
Will Yavlak
Arslan stand against Geyhatu's army?

789
01:50:54,086 --> 01:50:56,586
He sold us out to Osman...

790
01:50:56,653 --> 01:50:59,703
and he'll sell Osman out to Geyhatu.

791
01:50:59,848 --> 01:51:02,448
Kayıs will be in trouble.

792
01:51:05,448 --> 01:51:08,338
So, you're decided.

793
01:51:11,189 --> 01:51:14,419
So, you won't...

794
01:51:14,595 --> 01:51:16,285
stand back.

795
01:51:18,165 --> 01:51:22,165
May Allah give you power.

796
01:51:30,304 --> 01:51:31,834
Uncle...

797
01:51:35,577 --> 01:51:37,687
Is our agreement still valid?

798
01:51:39,250 --> 01:51:41,660
Yes, it is.

799
01:51:43,217 --> 01:51:44,547
It is.

800
01:51:48,384 --> 01:51:50,054
Good.

801
01:52:12,767 --> 01:52:14,727
What does it mean, Dündar Bey?

802
01:52:15,274 --> 01:52:17,724
What are you up to? Tell me.

803
01:52:22,060 --> 01:52:24,190
If my brother and Osman...

804
01:52:25,430 --> 01:52:27,070
are allies...

805
01:52:27,790 --> 01:52:30,670
it means everything has changed.

806
01:52:32,245 --> 01:52:34,895
Calm down, Hatun.

807
01:52:35,092 --> 01:52:36,142
Calm down.

808
01:52:37,569 --> 01:52:40,799
Everything is just as I want them to be.

809
01:52:41,639 --> 01:52:42,639
Tomorrow...

810
01:52:44,147 --> 01:52:46,717
Savcı will declare his Beyship.

811
01:52:46,861 --> 01:52:50,231
Bamsı and his Alps won't accept that.

812
01:52:51,990 --> 01:52:55,400
Then, we'll get rid of Bamsı or...

813
01:52:57,019 --> 01:52:59,129
Savcı.

814
01:52:59,244 --> 01:53:00,714
What about Osman?

815
01:53:01,926 --> 01:53:03,586
What about my brother?

816
01:53:07,708 --> 01:53:09,438
Pray to Allah that...

817
01:53:09,810 --> 01:53:13,810
I wish your brother didn't
raid Geyhatu's tribe.

818
01:53:15,195 --> 01:53:18,475
Or else, nobody can save him.

819
01:53:45,936 --> 01:53:47,906
I'll go to Kayı tribe tomorrow.

820
01:53:50,559 --> 01:53:52,879
And I'll take the Beyship relic.

821
01:53:57,184 --> 01:54:01,184
I'll make the Kayı Alps as one man.

822
01:54:07,001 --> 01:54:11,001
Then, with Yavlak Arslan...

823
01:54:12,703 --> 01:54:15,343
I'll fight Geyhatu.

824
01:54:18,859 --> 01:54:25,069
Then, I'll rip that dog Nikola
out of these lands!

825
01:54:43,690 --> 01:54:45,050
Eyvallah.

826
01:54:47,133 --> 01:54:48,363
Eyvallah.

827
01:54:57,826 --> 01:54:59,226
Come on.

828
01:55:51,370 --> 01:55:52,140
From now on...

829
01:55:52,696 --> 01:55:54,546
we are at a turning point.

830
01:55:56,440 --> 01:55:59,820
Tomorrow, I'll be the Bey of Kayı tribe or...

831
01:56:01,925 --> 01:56:04,325
I'll die.

832
01:56:05,572 --> 01:56:07,632
Your Alps are with you.

833
01:56:07,757 --> 01:56:10,227
You'll be safe and sound, my Bey.

834
01:56:10,501 --> 01:56:12,481
Bamsı brought his horses.

835
01:56:14,029 --> 01:56:17,329
Tomorrow he'll draw a sword to me.

836
01:56:17,558 --> 01:56:20,358
I know it.

837
01:56:20,673 --> 01:56:26,133
He can do anything to make Osman the Bey.

838
01:56:28,125 --> 01:56:30,585
I informed Bayhuca.

839
01:56:30,918 --> 01:56:34,748
If I die tomorrow, he'll protect our case.

840
01:56:37,469 --> 01:56:39,469
No sleeping tonight!

841
01:56:40,147 --> 01:56:42,727
They may act anytime!

842
01:56:46,598 --> 01:56:47,838
Tomorrow...

843
01:56:50,163 --> 01:56:52,563
be ready to shed brother blood.

844
01:56:58,824 --> 01:56:59,884
My Bey...

845
01:57:00,783 --> 01:57:03,143
Kayı tribe will fight itself?

846
01:57:03,384 --> 01:57:06,884
Osman wants to kill
you to become Kayı Bey.

847
01:57:06,980 --> 01:57:09,790
Your brother obeys our traditions, right?

848
01:57:09,927 --> 01:57:13,927
But if our traditions let you kill your
brother in case of a state issue...

849
01:57:14,342 --> 01:57:16,612
Osman will kill you.

850
01:57:17,756 --> 01:57:21,316
What I am saying is that before
Osman kills you...

851
01:57:21,350 --> 01:57:22,620
Enough!

852
01:57:24,474 --> 01:57:27,974
- Don't ever talk about it again.
- You have to do it Savcı Bey.

853
01:57:27,974 --> 01:57:31,534
Either Bala or I am going to
have to live it through.

854
01:57:34,864 --> 01:57:39,964
You decide that.
You decide whose heart will burn.

855
01:57:41,623 --> 01:57:45,983
- I won't kill my brother.
- States need blood to shed.

856
01:57:51,684 --> 01:57:53,034
States need...

857
01:57:53,730 --> 01:57:55,160
blood to shed.

858
01:58:11,952 --> 01:58:13,142
Aygül.

859
01:58:18,204 --> 01:58:20,114
My beautiful girl.

860
01:58:20,810 --> 01:58:23,560
Tomorrow is going to be like doomsday.

861
01:58:27,250 --> 01:58:31,760
Savcı will want to be the Bey.
We are going to resist.

862
01:58:33,996 --> 01:58:38,586
You should know that Dündar Bey
will probably be against us.

863
01:58:41,637 --> 01:58:45,237
I know that this is going to be hard
for you.

864
01:58:47,642 --> 01:58:51,642
You can just sit back if you wish.

865
01:58:53,879 --> 01:58:55,389
Mother.

866
01:58:57,026 --> 01:59:01,566
The conquerer of Kulucahisar Osman
Bey deserves to be the Bey.

867
01:59:03,144 --> 01:59:06,594
Whoever tries to take this right
away from him...

868
01:59:07,076 --> 01:59:09,366
will find me against them.

869
01:59:14,537 --> 01:59:17,927
Thank you Aygül, thank you.

870
01:59:21,046 --> 01:59:23,576
I don't have anything to lose.

871
01:59:27,023 --> 01:59:29,693
I'd rather die...

872
01:59:30,540 --> 01:59:32,520
to let them override Osman Bey's right.

873
01:59:39,330 --> 01:59:42,980
We are like sisters with Bala.

874
01:59:43,047 --> 01:59:47,047
If my Bala is standing up with Osman
Bey...

875
01:59:47,949 --> 01:59:50,399
I will support her too.

876
01:59:52,818 --> 01:59:55,268
Mashallah, my girls.

877
01:59:56,316 --> 01:59:58,666
Mashallah.

878
02:01:03,292 --> 02:01:04,652
Tomorrow...

879
02:01:05,725 --> 02:01:08,405
they will come to take your sword.

880
02:01:14,859 --> 02:01:17,219
They will gird on...

881
02:01:18,017 --> 02:01:20,367
your valuable sword.

882
02:01:24,615 --> 02:01:28,085
Who do you want?

883
02:01:28,823 --> 02:01:30,763
Tell me, my Bey.

884
02:01:32,081 --> 02:01:34,161
Tell Abdurrahman...

885
02:01:36,689 --> 02:01:38,579
his last...

886
02:01:39,292 --> 02:01:41,322
duty.

887
02:01:51,220 --> 02:01:54,810
We have a lot to do, Abdurrahman Ghazi!

888
02:01:56,655 --> 02:01:58,165
My Bey...

889
02:02:26,290 --> 02:02:28,120
The end is near.

890
02:02:29,107 --> 02:02:31,097
I want everyone to...

891
02:02:31,588 --> 02:02:35,218
know my decision.

892
02:02:36,027 --> 02:02:39,477
You should know so that
you can act like it.

893
02:02:40,565 --> 02:02:43,345
When
Ertuğrul Ghazi, son of Süleyman Shah...

894
02:02:43,703 --> 02:02:46,673
give his life relic...

895
02:02:47,440 --> 02:02:52,040
Osman, son of Ertuğrul Ghazi, I...

896
02:02:54,144 --> 02:02:56,234
will take his Beyship relic.

897
02:03:18,121 --> 02:03:23,281
We'll go to Ertuğrul Ghazi's tribe to
take his sword and Beyship relic.

898
02:03:24,461 --> 02:03:27,871
We won't stand back
whoever we come across.

899
02:03:29,367 --> 02:03:31,097
Your command, my Bey.

900
02:04:19,447 --> 02:04:22,367
- Where's Dündar Bey?
- He knew we were coming, my Bey.

901
02:04:52,462 --> 02:04:55,172
Won't you stay by me, brother?

902
02:05:08,853 --> 02:05:10,723
I'll stay here, brother.

903
02:05:10,981 --> 02:05:13,001
I'll see that if you draw sword...

904
02:05:13,683 --> 02:05:21,313
to my father's friend Bamsı Bey, aunt
Selcan, Aygül and Bala...

905
02:05:22,512 --> 02:05:24,742
to take the sword of my father.

906
02:06:00,139 --> 02:06:02,399
Osman Bey is coming!

907
02:06:03,003 --> 02:06:05,343
Osman Bey is coming!

908
02:06:33,764 --> 02:06:37,764
Until victory or death!

909
02:07:02,404 --> 02:07:03,764
Brother!

910
02:07:05,207 --> 02:07:07,817
I'm here! I'm here!

911
02:07:33,765 --> 02:07:35,705
Brothers...

912
02:07:42,232 --> 02:07:44,832
your brother is here...

913
02:07:45,071 --> 02:07:47,771
one step closer and...

914
02:07:50,485 --> 02:07:53,355
I'll cut your head off.

915
02:08:47,152 --> 02:08:48,822
Ertuğrul Bey...

916
02:08:50,330 --> 02:08:52,200
is dying...

917
02:11:08,885 --> 02:11:12,425
I'm the Bey of here...

918
02:11:14,159 --> 02:11:16,239
and this state belongs to me!

919
02:11:19,348 --> 02:11:32,378
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com